<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Bank Luebeck 1996 profit down.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank Luebeck 1996 profit down.</headline>
<dateline>LUEBECK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank Luebeck AG, a subsidiary of Deutsche Bank AG, said on Thursday its net profit fell to 50.6 million marks ($30.8 million) in 1996 from 54.7 million marks in 1995.</p>
<p>The bank also said it planned to raise capital by a nominal 1.37 million marks to 28.78 million marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
<p>($ = 1.641 German Marks)</p>
</text>
